# Goal Description

The goal is to create a new "Gold and Silver Correlation" section in the React frontend (`http://localhost:5173/`) that displays the analysis generated by the Django backend. This includes interactive charts for Gold Prediction, Silver Prediction, and their Correlation, as well as a tabular view of the historical predictions and actual prices.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (Django)

We will modify the existing ML script to save the prediction data in a structured JSON format, and then create a new API endpoint to serve this data to the frontend.

#### [MODIFY] [gold_silver_prediction.py](file:///c:/Users/Sahil/Desktop/bizmetric/bizmetric_sahil_fsd/ML_Stock_analysis/backend/ml_models/gold_silver_prediction.py)
 - Update [fetch_and_predict()](file:///c:/Users/Sahil/Desktop/bizmetric/bizmetric_sahil_fsd/ML_Stock_analysis/backend/ml_models/gold_silver_prediction.py#7-117) to save the combined historical and predicted data into a JSON file (`gold_silver_data.json`) alongside the CSV and PNG files.

#### [MODIFY] [views.py](file:///c:/Users/Sahil/Desktop/bizmetric/bizmetric_sahil_fsd/ML_Stock_analysis/backend/ml_models/views.py)
 - Create a new Django API view `GoldSilverAnalysisView` that reads the `gold_silver_data.json` file and returns it as a JSON response.

#### [NEW] [urls.py](file:///c:/Users/Sahil/Desktop/bizmetric/bizmetric_sahil_fsd/ML_Stock_analysis/backend/ml_models/urls.py)
 - Add routing for `gold-silver/` pointing to `GoldSilverAnalysisView`.

#### [MODIFY] [config/urls.py](file:///c:/Users/Sahil/Desktop/bizmetric/bizmetric_sahil_fsd/ML_Stock_analysis/backend/config/urls.py)
 - Include `ml_models.urls` under the path `api/ml_models/`.

---

### Frontend (React)

We will create a new React component using Recharts to visualize the data fetched from the new API endpoint, and add a toggle to switch between the 3 charts and the data table.

#### [NEW] [GoldSilverAnalysis.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Sahil/Desktop/bizmetric/bizmetric_sahil_fsd/ML_Stock_analysis/frontend/src/components/GoldSilverAnalysis.jsx)
 - Fetch data from `GET /api/ml_models/gold-silver/`.
 - Maintain state for the active view (`gold`, `silver`, or `correlation`).
 - Render 3 buttons for toggling the charts.
 - Render the corresponding Recharts `LineChart` or `ScatterChart` based on the active view.
 - Render a `<table>` below the chart displaying the yearly prices (`Year`, `Actual GLD`, `Predicted GLD`, `Actual SLV`, `Predicted SLV`).

#### [MODIFY] [Dashboard.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Sahil/Desktop/bizmetric/bizmetric_sahil_fsd/ML_Stock_analysis/frontend/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx)
 - Import and include the `<GoldSilverAnalysis />` component within the dashboard layout.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
1. Run `python manage.py runserver` to ensure the Django backend runs smoothly and the new `api/ml_models/gold-silver/` endpoint returns the JSON data.
2. Run `npm run dev` in the frontend directory to ensure the React app compiles without errors.

### Manual Verification
1. Open the browser to `http://localhost:5173/`.
2. Verify that the "Gold and Silver Correlation" section is visible.
3. Click through the "Gold", "Silver", and "Gold Silver Co-relation" buttons and ensure the Recharts graphs update interactively.
4. Verify the tabular data is displayed correctly at the bottom of the section.
